<title>USA: San Diego stadium expansion plan set for trial.</title>
<headline>San Diego stadium expansion plan set for trial.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO, Calif. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A California judge has set a February 20 trial date on San Diego's $78 million expansion and renovation of Jack Murphy stadium.</p>
<p>At the trial, Superior Court Judge Anthony Joseph is expected to decide the scope of an ordinance approved by the San Diego city council earlier this week.</p>
<p>The city maintains that ordinance rescinded an $18 million portion of the $78 million stadium project, Lauri Twomey, a spokeswoman for the city attorney's office, said Friday.</p>
<p>Opponents of the stadium plan argue that the ordinance effectively rescinded the entire $78 million expansion.  </p>
<p>The trial will be closely watched in San Diego.</p>
<p>If Joseph rules that the city council voided the entire project by rescinding the $18 million portion, the future for stadium expansion would be in serious doubt, Twomey said.</p>
<p>&quot;He's got our life in his hands,&quot; she said, referring to the judge.</p>
</text>
